alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The normalization_tables entry, invoked as `normalization_tables DIR` with DIR naming, relative to the working directory, a directory holding the Unicode 17.0.0 character database files UnicodeData.txt and DerivedNormalizationProps.txt. It reads every code point's canonical combining class and canonical decomposition mapping from UnicodeData.txt, recursively expands each canonical decomposition to its full (non-Hangul) form, reads Full_Composition_Exclusion from DerivedNormalizationProps.txt, and builds the primary canonical composition pairs from UnicodeData.txt's raw (one-step) two-code-point canonical decompositions that are not excluded. Hangul syllables (AC00..D7A3) are left out of every table and are composed and decomposed arithmetically at run time instead. It prints to standard output the Whitefoot source of thirteen const arrays: two-stage block tables, one entry per 256-code-point block naming which deduplicated block holds its entries, then each distinct block's entries once, and flat arrays addressed by a table's own id. ccc_block_index and ccc_block_bytes give the canonical combining class; decomposition_block_index and decomposition_block_ids name, per code point, an id into decomposition_offsets and decomposition_lengths, which locate its full decomposition in decomposition_values; composition_block_index and composition_block_ids name, per starter, an id into composition_offsets and composition_counts, which locate its pairs in composition_combining and composition_composed. It exits 0 after printing, 1 when an argument is missing, and 2 when a file cannot be read.";
